  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Voluntary Assisted Return and Reintegration Programme for Non-EEA Nationals (VARRP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will contribute to the Government of Ireland&#x2019;s comprehensive management of migration by providing return support to applicants in the international protection system, victims of trafficking and other vulnerable cases willing to return voluntarily to their countries of origin and support for their immediate reintegration. IOM Ireland will provide holistic assistance to beneficiaries of the programme through all stages from pre- departure to the post- departure and reintegration phases. The programme comprises four stages: information and outreach and referral into the programme; preparation for return including referral to psycho-social supports, virtual counselling, and preparatory training courses; return/travel phase including specialized supports for particularly vulnerable applicants including victims of trafficking; and reintegration support employing the virtual counselling service and expertise with referrals into local support networks.</narrative>
  </description>
